title: AbriLanternTale
---
Keeper: Venn wants a route that waits for us. My grandmother would have laughed at that. #emotion:Amused
Sela: Laughed? #emotion:Curious
Keeper: Tallow used to trade with a canyon town called Lanternwick. Their lanterns read the passages and guided ships along them. #emotion:Tender
Taren: Even passages that move? #emotion:Curious
Keeper: That was the whole trick. They stopped answering last season, but their course is still in our beacon, out through the Wick Reach. #emotion:Worried
Sela: A route that waits. That's Venn's third condition. #emotion:Determined
Taren: And the food? #emotion:Neutral
Sela: One impossible thing at a time, Vosk. #emotion:Playful
<<setFlag lantern.routeKnown>>
<<startQuest LanternRoad>>
===
title: AbriLanternRepeat
---
Keeper: The Wick Reach warp is off the approach, past the port marker. Bring me back a lantern story with a happy ending. #emotion:Tender
===
title: AbriLanternHome
---
Keeper: You brought back a lantern-keeper. Well, an apprentice. That's how it starts. #emotion:Happy
Sela: The chart answers every relay that's still lit. Tallow can follow its passage now. #emotion:Determined
Keeper: A route that waits. Venn will hate how pretty it is. #emotion:Amused
Taren: That's one of her three. Food and power are still on the list. #emotion:Worried
Sela: Pell says the river towns on Xylos move their farms with the floods. #emotion:Curious
Taren: Then food first. #emotion:Determined
<<setFlag chapter2.homecoming>>
===
title: SelaWickRelays
---
Sela: Those towers are relays. Old ones. And every one of them has been cut open. #emotion:Worried
Taren: Cut for what? #emotion:Curious
Sela: The glass in the crown. Somebody wants it badly enough to strip a whole chain. #emotion:Intense
Taren: Then somebody's still out here. Stay close. #emotion:Determined
===
title: AumiFirst
---
Aumi: That's close enough. The last crew that docked here left with three of my relays in their hold. #emotion:Angry
Taren: We're from Tallow Drift. We came for help, not glass. #emotion:Neutral
Aumi: Everyone comes for help. Then they come back for the glass. #emotion:Worried
Sela: Tallow is moving with its passage. Your relays used to guide stations like that. We need a way to follow it. #emotion:Determined
Aumi: Used to. The gorge relays are dark, and Muster scavengers are working in the dark beside them. #emotion:Intense
Aumi: Relight the three gorge relays and drive the scavengers out. Then I'll believe you came to give something back. #emotion:Determined
Taren: Where's the way down? #emotion:Curious
Aumi: Orchard gate, west terrace. Grazers hate light, and so do the Muster. Use that. #emotion:Neutral
===
title: AumiRepeat
---
Aumi: Three relays. The gorge gate is past the orchard. Light first, then glass. That's the order here. #emotion:Neutral
===
title: AumiReturn
---
Aumi: The gorge is lit. I could see it from the stair. #emotion:Shocked
Taren: Their captain is under guard at the relay. Your keepers have her. #emotion:Neutral
Aumi: Then you've done what the last three visitors only promised. #emotion:Tender
Aumi: Ishen opened the archive while you were down there. Read the wall. It's been waiting longer than any of us. #emotion:Determined
Sela: Those light patterns are passages. Moving ones. And there are towns travelling beside them. #emotion:Shocked
Aumi: When the roads last left, most of our ancestors went with them. The rest kept the lanterns lit for anyone who came back. #emotion:Tender
Aumi: Take this chart. Every relay that still burns will answer it. A route that waits, as your director put it. #emotion:Determined
<<setFlag lanternwick.chartGiven>>
Aumi: And take Pell. Someone should keep a lantern lit on that station of yours. #emotion:Amused
===
title: AumiFinal
---
Aumi: Go on. The relays know you now. Come back with a story worth adding to the wall. #emotion:Tender
===
title: PellFirst
---
Pell: You flew in? Actually flew? Not in a ship, as the ship? #emotion:Shocked
Sela: As the ship. Mind the vanes. #emotion:Playful
Pell: I'm Pell. I keep the lamps on the lower stair, which means I climb the lower stair forty times a day. #emotion:Happy
Pell: Don't let Aumi scare you off. She's only like that with people. #emotion:Amused
===
title: PellRepeat
---
Pell: If you see a lamp out on the stair, tell me. If you see a grazer, don't tell me. Just run. #emotion:Playful
===
title: PellLampOffer
---
Pell: Are you going back down the gorge? Can I ask you something? Quietly? #emotion:Worried
Pell: I dropped my lamp down there. Not dropped. A grazer took it, and I ran, and the lamp didn't. #emotion:Flustered
Pell: It was my mother's. Aumi doesn't know it's gone. There's a den under the fallen tower, past the second relay. #emotion:Worried
Taren: We'll look for it. #emotion:Tender
<<startQuest PellsLamp>>
===
title: PellLampReturn
---
Taren: One lamp. Slightly chewed. #emotion:Amused
Pell: You found it! It still lights. Look at that, it still lights. #emotion:Happy
Pell: Don't tell Aumi. Actually, do tell her. Tell her I'm the one who sent you. #emotion:Playful
<<setFlag pell.lampReturned>>
===
title: PellPost
---
Pell: Aumi says I'm going with you. To Tallow. On a station that moves. #emotion:Shocked
Pell: I've packed four times. I keep unpacking the lamp to check it still works. #emotion:Happy
===
title: IshenFirst
---
Ishen: Visitors, and not the kind with cutting torches. Come in. Mind the record. #emotion:Happy
Ishen: I'm Ishen. I keep the archive, which means I keep the light patterns, which means I read walls for a living. #emotion:Amused
Taren: What's on the walls? #emotion:Curious
Ishen: Passages. Thousands of them, recorded by lantern over more years than this canyon has names for. #emotion:Tender
Ishen: Three record plates went missing in the Sunken Relay below the gorge. If you go down there, bring back any you find. #emotion:Determined
<<startQuest IshensRecord>>
===
title: IshenRepeat
---
Ishen: Three plates, palm-sized, cut with circles. If they look like coasters, they probably aren't coasters. #emotion:Amused
===
title: IshenRecordReturn
---
Ishen: All three. You have no idea what you're holding. Well, neither do I yet. Give me a moment. #emotion:Shocked
Ishen: These came from Oriel, a world that tried to hold a passage still the last time the roads left. #emotion:Worried
Ishen: It says the passage fought the cage. It says the world broke around it. #emotion:Sad
Sela: The Muster were stripping relay glass down there. Do they know about this? #emotion:Worried
Ishen: I hope not. I'll keep these where nobody with a torch can find them. #emotion:Determined
<<setFlag ishen.recordRestored>>
===
title: IshenPost
---
Ishen: The archive's lit again. Come back when you've seen something worth writing down. #emotion:Tender
===
title: CorraFirst
---
Corra: Fresh faces, fresh scrip. Corra Vey, arch market. I sell lamp oil, parts and advice, and the advice is free. #emotion:Happy
Corra: Here's some: don't argue with Aumi before breakfast. #emotion:Amused
-> Show us what you have.
    <<shop>>
-> Maybe later.
    Corra: Later's fine. Later still pays. #emotion:Smug
===
title: CorraRepeat
---
Corra: Light, parts, and more light. What do you need? #emotion:Happy
<<shop>>
===
title: CorraPost
---
Corra: Brekk ate. Then he fixed my awning without asking. I might keep him. #emotion:Amused
<<shop>>
===
title: CorraRationsOffer
---
Corra: You've been down the gorge. Did you see the scavengers' camp? #emotion:Worried
Taren: We saw it. #emotion:Neutral
Corra: They keep ration crates by the fire. Muster rations. Ugly, but they keep. #emotion:Neutral
Corra: Bring one to the orchard shed. Someone in there can't eat our food, and he's too proud to steal theirs. #emotion:Worried
Taren: Someone? #emotion:Curious
Corra: Knock twice. Don't stare. #emotion:Determined
<<startQuest UnswornRations>>
===
title: BrekkFirst
---
Brekk: You're not Muster. Good. Then you didn't see me. #emotion:Worried
Taren: We're not looking for anyone. #emotion:Neutral
Brekk: Everyone who comes up that canyon is looking for someone. Close the door on your way out. #emotion:Neutral
===
title: BrekkRepeat
---
Brekk: Still here. Still not seen. #emotion:Neutral
===
title: BrekkRations
---
Taren: From Corra, by way of the scavengers' camp. #emotion:Neutral
Brekk: Muster rations. I swore I'd never eat these again. #emotion:Sad
Brekk: I was a smith at the Bridle works. I made cages for a living until I couldn't stand it. Then I walked. #emotion:Worried
Sela: Cages for what? #emotion:Curious
Brekk: For roads. For the creatures you fly through. The Muster wants to leash them like beasts and own every world they reach. #emotion:Intense
Brekk: Thank Corra for me. And if you meet the people I left behind, tell them some of us stopped. #emotion:Tender
<<setFlag unsworn.rationsDelivered>>
===
title: BrekkPost
---
Brekk: Corra has me fixing awnings. First honest metal I've touched in years. #emotion:Tender
===
title: SelaRelayLit
---
Sela: It's taking the charge. Look, the glass remembers its pattern. #emotion:Shocked
Taren: The grazers are backing off. #emotion:Curious
Sela: Light first. Aumi wasn't being poetic. #emotion:Amused
===
title: SelaSunkenRelay
---
Taren: This was a relay station. A whole station, under the canyon. #emotion:Curious
Sela: Fresh cuts on the lantern housings. They're still down here, Vosk. #emotion:Worried
Taren: Then let's be quieter than they are. #emotion:Determined
===
title: HessaConfront
---
Hessa: Shapers. Out here. Somebody's paying you better than they pay me. #emotion:Smug
Taren: Nobody's paying us. Put the glass down. #emotion:Determined
Hessa: When the roads go, every world left behind will need someone to answer to. The Muster intends to be that someone. #emotion:Intense
Hessa: This glass helps. Your lantern-keeper's feelings don't. #emotion:Smug
Sela: So that's a no. #emotion:Playful
Hessa: That's a no. #emotion:Angry
<<setFlag relay.hessaConfronted>>
===
title: HessaYields
---
Hessa: Enough. Enough! You've made your point, Shapers. #emotion:Angry
Taren: Keep your hands where the keepers can see them. #emotion:Determined
Hessa: You think one canyon matters? The Warmaster has a hundred crews like mine, and none of them lose sleep over lanterns. #emotion:Smug
Sela: Then they'll lose it over something else. #emotion:Determined
<<setFlag relay.hessaYielded>>
===
title: HessaRepeat
---
Hessa: The keepers have me. Go and gloat somewhere with better light. #emotion:Smug
===
